---
import StudyLayout from "../../../layouts/StudyLayout.astro";
---

<StudyLayout>
  <section>
    <h1>Inhabited worlds · question test</h1>
    <p>
      15 November 2026. Independent, clean-context, read-only review of the
      <a href="/lab/studies/inhabited-worlds-2026-11-15">opening</a>, registry,
      study contract and relevant specifications and code.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Metric</th>
          <th>Result</th>
          <th>Reason</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>One subject</td>
          <td>Pass</td>
          <td>
            One visual language for inhabited atmospheric worlds; Earth and
            fictional geography are instances. Mercury and Venus own different
            treatments and serve as current context.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Grounded</td>
          <td>Pass with findings</td>
          <td>
            Art direction, controls, gravity and contact have standing contracts
            and implementation. Clarify which contact behaviour and current
            scene baseline remain fixed.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Consequence</td>
          <td>Pass</td>
          <td>
            One composed flight-scale Lab demonstration changes; production
            integration and atmospheric rules are adjacent.
          </td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <h2>Findings and responses</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Contact:</strong>
      the gravity contract specifies bounce and hull damage; Practice holds hull
      full. Section 01 now fixes solid-body contact motion rather than implying
      one damage rule across modes. Evidence:
      <code>docs/specs/game/world/gravity-field/spec.md</code>,
      <code>docs/specs/game/test-flight/spec.md</code>,
      <code>packages/core/src/lib/physics/Physics.ts</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Baseline:</strong>
      named Mercury and Venus materials belong to Practice. Section 01 now names
      Practice G7, Mercury, Venus and starter Wasp. Evidence:
      <code>docs/specs/game/world/planets/spec.md</code>
      and
      <code>apps/web/src/components/FlightDeck.svelte</code>. Both corrections
      were made after review and were not retested.
    </p>
    <h2>Other grounding and limits</h2>
    <p>
      <code>docs/design.md</code>
      supports economical forms and distinct material languages. The controls
      contract and <code>packages/core/src/lib/entities/Input.ts</code>
      establish input; the gravity contract and Physics implementation establish
      summed mass-well pulls and cut-off. The planet contract explicitly gives
      Venus's atmosphere no collision, drag or damage region.
    </p>
    <p>
      The registry was checked for overlap. No stopped Earth page, review,
      evidence, reference, sketch or asset was read; only registry metadata was
      used for the ownership check. Browser rendering, visual quality, gameplay,
      future feasibility and performance were not checked. This is a question
      test, not design acceptance.
    </p>
  </section>
</StudyLayout>
<style>
th,
td {
  text-align: left;
  vertical-align: top;
  padding: 0.6rem 1rem 0.6rem 0;
}
</style>
